            <ArticleTitle>[Chest pain in a 37-year-old Sikh].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>99-102</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chest pain can be the only sign of osteomalacia. The case of a 37 years old patient from India, member of the religious group of the sikh, with vitamin D deficiency is presented. The disease developed as a consequence of reduced sun exposure (covering a substantial part of the body for ethnic reasons). The pathogenesis, clinical picture and implications for daily practice are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
